      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Stepping out into the winter cold, Ilona immediately dials Khanikeyev to report on her unexpected inspection. Convinced that the kindergarten is completely ordinary despite its quirky staff, she tells him not to worry. Inside, the undercover agents celebrate avoiding detection and dismiss their disguised operative. Let's listen to this concluding phone call in Russian first; don't worry about catching every word.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Алло, Ханикеев! Ты зря волновался.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "В детском саду всё нормально.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "khanikeev",
      "t": "Ты уверена? Там нет полиции?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Воспитатель, конечно, немного странный.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но они там все такие.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Так что спи спокойно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "khanikeev",
      "t": "Хорошо. Большое спасибо за помощь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пожалуйста. Я еду домой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Она уехала? Всё чисто?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Ну вот, нормально всё прошло?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Она ничего не поняла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Операция прошла отлично!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Ты свободен, Гриша.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Иди отдыхай после танцев.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let us walk through this concluding phone debrief and undercover relief step by step.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Алло, Ханикеев! Ты зря волновался.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hello, Khanikeyev! You were worried for nothing.' The adverb meaning in vain reassures the anxious caller.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "В детском саду всё нормально.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'At the kindergarten everything is fine.' The short adjective form functions as a standard neutral predicate.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "khanikeev",
      "t": "Ты уверена? Там нет полиции?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Are you sure? There is no police there?' The feminine short adjective expresses certainty.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Воспитатель, конечно, немного странный.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The teacher, of course, is a bit strange.' The parenthetical word indicates natural concession.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но они там все такие.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But they are all like that there.' The demonstrative pronoun in the plural refers back to eccentric nursery staff.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Так что спи спокойно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'So sleep peacefully.' The conjunctional phrase introduces a reassuring logical conclusion.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "khanikeev",
      "t": "Хорошо. Большое спасибо за помощь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Good. Thank you very much for your help.' The preposition meaning 'for' takes the accusative case form.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пожалуйста. Я еду домой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are welcome. I am driving home.' The verb of vehicular motion expresses current purposeful travel.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Она уехала? Всё чисто?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did she leave? Is everything clear?' The short form adjective conveys that the coast is clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Ну вот, нормально всё прошло?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well now, did everything go fine?' The introductory particle sequence marks a satisfied summation.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Она ничего не поняла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She understood nothing.' Russian employs double negation with the negative pronoun and particle.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Операция прошла отлично!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The operation went excellently!' The past tense feminine verb agrees with the feminine noun.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Ты свободен, Гриша.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are free, Grisha.' The short adjective expresses release from operational duty.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Иди отдыхай после танцев.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Go rest after the dancing.' The preposition meaning 'after' governs the genitive plural noun ending. Now let us listen to the complete scene once more, contrasting the phone call with the team's relief.",
      "gap": 0.9
